<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Basay</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Basay people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Basay were an Austronesian indigenous people of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a>, living around the harbours of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keelung">Keelung</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamsui">Tamsui</a> and along the north-east coast. Known as traders, metalworkers and boatmen, they dealt with Chinese and Japanese merchants and later with the Spanish, who settled among them from 1626, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>. Under Qing rule they were gradually assimilated, and their language is now extinct.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/basay.jpg" alt="Basay" width="320" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 鳥居龍藏 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:At_the_Kanatsui_tribe_of_Basay_people_in_Taihoku.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
